  "opennyai_summary": {
    "PREAMBLE": "State vs Mohd. Moies on 11 December, 2024\nIn The Court Of Sh. Sukhjeet Singh, Judicial Magistrate\n First Class , South District, Saket Courts, Delhi\n State Vs. Mohd Moies\n Fir No. : 618/2016\n Ps : Hauz Khas\n U/s : 506/509 Ipc\n Judgment\nA. Sl. No. of the Case 2039607/2016 B.\nDate of Commission of offence 12.08.2016 D.\nDate of charge-sheet 18.11.2016 E.\nName of the complainant Smt. Apurvaa Mehta F.\nName of the accused persons, Mohd. Moies S/o Irshad Ahmad, R/o their parentage and residence Sector 43, Rama Apartments, Gurgaon Haryana G.\nOffence complained of or proved 506/509 IPC H.\nDate of framing of charge 10.01.2018 I.\nPlea of the accused Not guilty J.\nDate on which judgment is 27.11.2024 reserved K.\nFinal Order Acquitted L. Date of Judgment 10.12.2024\nState Vs. Mohd. Moies FIR No. : 618/2016 PS Hauz Khas U/s 506/509 IPC Page no.1 of 6 Brief facts of the present case 1.\n",
    "facts": "The case of the prosecution is that on 11.08.2016 at about 11 pm during telephonic conversation of accused with complainant Ms. Aporva Mehta, accused intending to insult the modesty of the complainant, uttered abuses to her and also threatened to kill her.\nThereafter FIR was registered in the case.\nAfter completing the investigation, charge-sheet was filed against accused.\nFraming of charge 2.\nHe brought the original FIR registration of year 2016.\n",
    "ANALYSIS": "The offence of insulting the modesty of a woman is a cognizable, bailable, and compoundable offence.\nBefore the Criminal Law (Amendment) Act, 2013, the offence was punishable with simple imprisonment, which may extend to one year, or with a fine, or both.\nIn the present case, it is defence of the accused that accused and the complainant used to work in the same company namely India Medtronic Pvt Ltd and both of them were in relationship with each other and complainant used to exchange love messages with the accused and when accused refused to marry then the complainant filed a false case of rape i.e. FIR NO. 623/2016 and the present case.\nIn the present case, in the absence of testimony of complainant who is the star witness, the allegations alleged against the accused are not proved in the present case and testimony of IO and perusal of document Ex.PW3/C also somehow points out towards the fact that the present case is false and fabricated and filed just to implicate the accused person due to the refusal of marriage.\nIt is well settled that in a criminal trial the burden of proof is on the prosecution to prove its case beyond reasonable doubt.\nAny contradiction or iota of proof in favour of accused can completely dismantle the case of prosecution.\nIn the present case there are no cogent material available on record to suggest that accused had insulted the modesty of complainant and threatened to kill her.\nThe allegations against accused are not proved in the case.\n",
    "decision": "In these circumstances and in view of the aforementioned discussion, I hold that the prosecution has failed to prove its case against the accused Mohd. Moies beyond reasonable doubts.\nAccused Mohd. Moies is accordingly acquitted for offence u/s 506/509 IPC.\n"
  },
